{"ref":"BDB, מָעוֹן²","hw":"מָעוֹן²","html":"† I. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">מָעוֹן</span></big>  <strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>refuge</strong>, hence <strong>habitation</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 71:3\" href=\"/Psalms.71.3\">ψ 71:3</a> +, cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְעוֹן</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 25:30\" href=\"/Jeremiah.25.30\">Je 25:30</a> +, sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְעוֹנֶ֑ךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 91:9\" href=\"/Psalms.91.9\">ψ 91:9</a>, etc.;—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <em>lair</em> of jackals <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 9:10\" href=\"/Jeremiah.9.10\">Je 9:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 10:22\" href=\"/Jeremiah.10.22\">10:22</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 49:33\" href=\"/Jeremiah.49.33\">49:33</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 51:37\" href=\"/Jeremiah.51.37\">51:37</a> (all of desolated cities); <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ אֲרָיוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Nahum 2:12\" href=\"/Nahum.2.12\">Na 2:12</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">מִרְעֶה</span>; fig. of Nineveh).<br><strong>2.</strong>  <em>dwelling</em> of <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span>: <strong>a.</strong>  in heaven <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ קָדְשְׁךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 26:15\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.26.15\">Dt 26:15</a> cf. <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 25:30\" href=\"/Jeremiah.25.30\">Je 25:30</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">מָרוֹם</span>), <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 2:17\" href=\"/Zechariah.2.17\">Zc 2:17</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 68:6\" href=\"/Psalms.68.6\">ψ 68:6</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 30:27\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.30.27\">2 Ch 30:27</a>. <strong>b.</strong>  in temple <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ בֵּיתֶ֑ךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 26:8\" href=\"/Psalms.26.8\">ψ 26:8</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">מְעוֹנוֹ</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 36:15\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.36.15\">2 Ch 36:15</a> (only here alone).<br><strong>3.</strong>  fig. of <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> as refuge of his people, <span dir=\"rtl\">צוּר מ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 71:3\" href=\"/Psalms.71.3\">ψ 71:3</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> alone <a data-ref=\"Psalms 90:1\" href=\"/Psalms.90.1\">90:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 91:9\" href=\"/Psalms.91.9\">91:9</a>.—<span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 2:29\" href=\"/I_Samuel.2.29\">1 S 2:29</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 2:32\" href=\"/I_Samuel.2.32\">32</a> is unintelling. (v. Comm.), poss. read <span dir=\"rtl\">מְעוֹיֵן</span> (<em>eyeing</em> [enviously], v. <a data-ref=\"BDB, עִין\" href=\"/BDB,_עִין\", dir=\"rtl\">עין</a> denom.) Klo HPS, cf. 𝔊 Bu. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְעוֹנָהּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Zephaniah 3:7\" href=\"/Zephaniah.3.7\">Zp 3:7</a> is difficult in context, 𝔊 We Now read <span dir=\"rtl\">מֵעֵינֶיה</span> (cf. <a data-ref=\"Joshua 9:23\" href=\"/Joshua.9.23\">Jos 9:23</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 3:29\" href=\"/II_Samuel.3.29\">2 S 3:29</a>).","next":"BDB, מָעוֹן³","prev":"BDB, עוּן"}